  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Establishment of an AI and Satellite-based Climate-Intelligent Monitoring Solution to Enhance Climate Resilience in the Philippine Agriculture Sector</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Localization and Enhancement of DI Cast Using Philippine Datasets  Through this project DI Labs AI based climate risk monitoring and forecasting platform, DI Cast, will be localized and enhanced to reflect the climatic and geographical characteristics of the Philippines. To achieve this, rainfall observation data from the Philippine Atmospheric, Geophysical and Astronomical Services Administration (PAGASA) will be collected and refined, then combined with high-resolution geostationary satellite imagery such as that from GEO-KOMPSAT-2A for retraining the AIRadar model The enhanced model will improve the accuracy of rainfall estimation and expand spatial coverage beyond the limitations of traditional numerical models and ground radar systems enabling effective application nationwide The upgraded version of DI Cast will be designed to support real time forecasting and hazard detection accessible to public institutions and local communities</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to enhance climate adaptation and disaster response capacity in the Philippine agricultural sector which is highly vulnerable to climate related disasters  The project will conduct a local Proof of Concept PoC of DI Cast  an AI and satellite based intelligent climate monitoring solution developed by DILab and establish a high resolution climate information delivery system The Philippines faces recurring typhoons heavy rainfall and droughts that threaten agricultural productivity and food security These challenges are exacerbated in rural and island regions where ground based weather observation infrastructure is severely limited leading to inadequate access to timely and accurate climate information&#xbcf8; &#xc0ac;&#xc5c5;&#xc740; &#xc778;&#xacf5;&#xc9c0;&#xb2a5;(AI)&#xacfc; &#xc704;&#xc131; &#xae30;&#xbc18; &#xae30;&#xd6c4; &#xac10;&#xc2dc; &#xc194;&#xb8e8;&#xc158;&#xc778; DI Cast&#xb97c; &#xd65c;&#xc6a9;&#xd558;&#xc5ec;, &#xae30;&#xd6c4;&#xc7ac;&#xd574;&#xc5d0; &#xcde8;&#xc57d;&#xd55c; &#xd544;&#xb9ac;&#xd540;&#xc758; &#xae30;&#xd6c4; &#xc704;&#xd5d8; &#xb300;&#xc751; &#xc5ed;&#xb7c9;&#xc744; &#xac15;&#xd654;&#xd558;&#xace0;, &#xb18d;&#xc5c5; &#xbd84;&#xc57c;&#xc758; &#xc758;&#xc0ac;&#xacb0;&#xc815; &#xccb4;&#xacc4; &#xace0;&#xb3c4;&#xd654; &#xbc0f; &#xae30;&#xd6c4;&#xc815;&#xbcf4; &#xc811;&#xadfc;&#xc131; &#xd615;&#xd3c9;&#xc131; &#xc81c;&#xace0;&#xb97c; &#xbaa9;&#xd45c;&#xb85c; &#xd55c;&#xb2e4;. 
&#x25a3; &#xc774;&#xb97c; &#xc704;&#xd574; &#xd604;&#xc9c0; &#xae30;&#xc0c1;&#xccad; &#xbc0f; &#xad00;&#xb828; &#xae30;&#xad00;&#xc73c;&#xb85c;&#xbd80;&#xd130; 1&#xb144; &#xc774;&#xc0c1; &#xae30;&#xac04;&#xc758; &#xac15;&#xc218; &#xb370;&#xc774;&#xd130;&#xb97c; &#xc218;&#xc9d1;&#xd558;&#xace0;, &#xc704;&#xc131; &#xc601;&#xc0c1;&#xacfc; &#xc815;&#xd569;&#xd558;&#xc5ec; AI &#xd559;&#xc2b5;&#xc6a9; &#xb370;&#xc774;&#xd130;&#xc14b;&#xc744; &#xad6c;&#xcd95;&#xd55c;&#xb2e4;. &#xd574;&#xb2f9; &#xb370;&#xc774;&#xd130;&#xb97c; &#xbc14;&#xd0d5;&#xc73c;&#xb85c; &#xae30;&#xc874; &#xd55c;&#xad6d;&#xd615; AI-radar &#xbaa8;&#xb378;&#xc744; &#xc9c0;&#xc5ed; &#xd2b9;&#xc131;&#xc5d0; &#xb9de;&#xcdb0; &#xc7ac;&#xd559;&#xc2b5;&#xd558;&#xba70;, &#xac15;&#xc218; &#xc720;&#xd615; &#xbc0f; &#xacc4;&#xc808;&#xc131;&#xc5d0; &#xb530;&#xb77c; &#xc608;&#xce21; &#xc815;&#xd655;&#xb3c4;&#xb97c; &#xbd84;&#xc11d;&#xd558;&#xace0; &#xace0;&#xb3c4;&#xd654;&#xd55c;&#xb2e4;. DI Cast&#xb294; &#xd604;&#xc9c0; &#xc0ac;&#xc6a9;&#xc790;&#xb4e4;&#xc774; &#xc27d;&#xac8c; &#xc811;&#xadfc;&#xd560; &#xc218; &#xc788;&#xb3c4;&#xb85d; &#xd604;&#xc9c0;&#xc5b4; UI&#xc640; &#xbaa8;&#xbc14;&#xc77c; &#xce5c;&#xd654;&#xd615; &#xc778;&#xd130;&#xd398;&#xc774;&#xc2a4;&#xb97c; &#xd3ec;&#xd568;&#xd55c; &#xae30;&#xb2a5;&#xc744; &#xcd94;&#xac00;&#xd55c;&#xb2e4;.</narrative>
  </description>
